source:
/**
 * 语义键 → 目标列表。三态：非空列表是已绑定，空列表是显式不支持，键缺失是从未推断。
 */

translation:
/**
 * Semantic key → target list. Three states: a nonempty list means bound, an empty list means explicitly unsupported, and an absent key means never inferred.
 */

/**
 * Manual splitting actions: cut, split, move boundary, merge with next episode, clear subsequent cuts. Offsets are code point offsets within `source_file`;
 * when `source_file` is omitted, split uses the file containing the episode start, and move boundary uses the file containing its end.
 */

/**
 * Structure for referring to entries outside the episode page (backend `with_episode_item_refs`): entry IDs are not shown to creators;
 * the UI formats them as "Title · 5", using the broadcast position when the title is empty.
 */

/**
 * Output audio track mode, matching `packages/arcreel-market-core/src/arcreel_market_core/video_backend_contract.py::VideoAudioMode` exactly:
 * `controllable` = the request carries an audio switch that forwards the user's on/off choice to the provider; `always_on` = always has audio, without a switch;
 * `always_off` = this route produces no audio track and has no switch. The server derives all three states from backend declarations; the frontend does not synthesize them.
 */

/**
 * Provider model status flags: `discontinued` is offline; `retiring` is due to go offline (see `lifecycle` for the shutdown date);
 * `unpriced` records call costs as unpriced; `modified` means the user changed the corresponding model information, which no longer follows official updates.
 */

/**
 * Lifecycle of the entry matched to the provider model as of today (UTC date). `successor` is the official successor's "model maker/official model name";
 * models without a matching entry are `available`, with null dates and successor.
 */

/**
   * The app version meets `min_app_version`. Models that do not meet it are placed at the end, disabled, excluded from defaults and candidates, and cannot be called;
   * they cannot be enabled and have no model settings to open.
   */

/**
 * Parameters supported by this provider (GET /providers/{id}/models/{model}):
 * `base` is the runtime value without overrides (evaluated from the catalog entry and backend); `null` means neither declares it (unrecorded);
 * `overrides` contains active capability overrides; `effective` contains effective values after overrides; `editable` lists editable dimensions in UI order,
 * empty for officially listed models; `displayed` lists all displayed dimensions in UI order, with dimensions outside `editable` read-only.
 */

/**
 * A manually entered new entry (a model absent from the catalog): missing `facts` fields use media-type defaults, and omitted `display_name` uses the model name;
 * `price` is a price table in catalog data format; omission records call costs as unpriced.
 */

/**
   * Project-level target episode duration preference (seconds), null when unset. The review panel uses it to compare episode total / target;
   * exceeding the target produces a notice without blocking confirmation or subsequent generation.
   */

/**
   * Ordered storyboard-level speech: character dialogue and voiceover in temporal order. New structure (drama);
   * legacy drama uses backend read-time migration, so this field may be absent when read by the frontend.
   */

/**
 * Final rendering of one prompt side. Exactly one of `text` and `unavailable` is non-null;
 * `unavailable` is already rendered by the backend in the request language and is not translated again by the frontend.
 */

/**
 * Models (provider/model) automatically selected by the backend when all project and global layers are unset for each purpose, matching execution-time resolution;
 * null when no provider is available. Text tiers share the same automatic inference and are combined into one entry.
 */

/**
 * Closed set of next-action identifiers returned by the backend, corresponding exactly to `WorkflowActionType` in `lib/workflow/workflow_state.py`;
 * backend contract tests keep both sides synchronized. A runtime array rather than just a type lets translation coverage
 * checks iterate every action: adding an action without copy fails the test instead of silently using fallback wording.
 */

/**
 * One notice in the plan. `code` is a stable machine key localized by the UI; `params` provides copy parameters;
 * raw reason text is not sent. Each notice appears only in its own step (project-level notices are at the top level), without duplication.
 */

/**
 * Admission result for the whole batch. Both outcomes other than `admitted` mean **no tasks were created**;
 * the UI must state this explicitly rather than merely reporting a failure.
 */

/**
 * What the last migration adjusted (`adjusted`) or could not carry over (`skipped`). Informational only, without affecting state or blocking;
 * production status includes it only when the report is nonempty and not yet acknowledged by the user. Failed project migrations use `project_migration_failed` in `blockers`.
 */

/**
 * Production status: current content (`content` / `artifacts`), admission for each AI operation (`operations`), and the suggested next action
 * (`next_action`, with parallel branch choices in `next_alternatives`). `blockers` only indicates that the project as a whole is unavailable;
 * data problems in the content itself belong in `issues`.
 */

/**
 * Request to open a video unit preview (from a unit link in an Agent reply): bring the preview forward when it is in a subtab on narrow screens;
 * when `seconds` is not null, start playback from that time. One-shot: cleared after the player consumes it, and expires if not consumed in time.
 */

/**
 * Move `episode` after `after` (null means first): `noop` leaves order unchanged; `locked` would violate source order between extracted episodes;
 * otherwise `ok`. Episodes with their own source or no source can go anywhere. The server rechecks resulting source ranges.
 */
